[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:00:16,615 --> 00:00:18,145
I guess so.

2
00:00:20,025 --> 00:00:24,314
It‘s really hitting me
that I'm dating a girl.

3
00:00:24,315 --> 00:00:25,855
It feels nice.

4
00:00:32,445 --> 00:00:33,445
I don't know,

5
00:00:34,625 --> 00:00:35,625
I'm thinking,

6
00:00:37,045 --> 00:00:41,375
I'm really happy right now.

7
00:00:47,105 --> 00:00:50,375
Am I really happy?

8
00:01:42,405 --> 00:01:49,905
"How Do We Relationship?"

9
00:01:54,905 --> 00:02:00,405
(Episode 1: I'll Go Out With You)

10
00:02:03,985 --> 00:02:06,365
The basketball club is a blast!
Come check us out!

11
00:02:06,885 --> 00:02:09,805
We're the science club! We do lots
of fun stuff. Please come check us out!

12
00:02:10,985 --> 00:02:16,465
If you don't join a club,
you'll never make any friends.

13
00:02:19,765 --> 00:02:21,335
Sorry. Excuse me.

14
00:02:23,605 --> 00:02:24,905
Are you okay?

15
00:02:25,685 --> 00:02:26,905
I'm fine.

16
00:02:28,115 --> 00:02:29,465
They're really shoving these flyers at us.

17
00:02:29,485 --> 00:02:32,085
Seriously. They hand out so
many just for them to get tossed.

18
00:02:36,845 --> 00:02:38,785
Thank you.

19
00:02:41,725 --> 00:02:42,725
Wow.

20
00:02:42,845 --> 00:02:44,155
Nice cleavage.

21
00:02:53,045 --> 00:02:54,574
That's so bad.

22
00:02:54,575 --> 00:02:56,305
First day of school.

23
00:02:58,545 --> 00:03:00,904
It is what it is.

24
00:03:00,905 --> 00:03:02,115
It was right in front of my face.

25
00:03:03,185 --> 00:03:05,205
Hey, knock it off.

26
00:03:05,925 --> 00:03:08,191
- One more time! One more time!
- That short-haired girl is pretty cute, right?

27
00:03:08,215 --> 00:03:10,985
Totally my type.

28
00:03:12,945 --> 00:03:13,945
What's their deal?

29
00:03:15,145 --> 00:03:16,145
Hey.

30
00:03:16,265 --> 00:03:19,004
Miwa, be honest.
You're actually super popular, aren't you?

31
00:03:19,005 --> 00:03:20,665
How many boyfriends have you had so far?

32
00:03:21,535 --> 00:03:22,535
Huh?

33
00:03:23,525 --> 00:03:24,395
Where did that come from?

34
00:03:24,396 --> 00:03:26,265
I'm just curious.

35
00:03:28,965 --> 00:03:31,005
Well...

36
00:03:32,405 --> 00:03:33,405
Well?

37
00:03:34,565 --> 00:03:35,565
Ah...

38
00:03:35,885 --> 00:03:36,885
It's not that.

39
00:03:37,025 --> 00:03:38,025
Um...

40
00:03:38,125 --> 00:03:39,125
How should I put this?

41
00:03:39,485 --> 00:03:41,015
I don't know if it counts as dating.

42
00:03:41,665 --> 00:03:44,624
We were supposedly dating,
but it was kind of a situationship.

43
00:03:44,625 --> 00:03:45,824
Huh?

44
00:03:45,825 --> 00:03:46,825
Like, it's complicated?

45
00:03:46,826 --> 00:03:48,395
Like, I shouldn't pry?

46
00:03:48,405 --> 00:03:51,025
Yeah... let's go with that.

47
00:03:52,465 --> 00:03:54,795
Miwa, you're amazing.

48
00:03:55,265 --> 00:03:57,765
You look like you could
bag any guy you want.

49
00:03:58,935 --> 00:04:01,535
That's not true at all.

50
00:04:02,835 --> 00:04:03,835
I...

51
00:04:04,545 --> 00:04:07,405
I've never actually had
my feelings reciprocated.

52
00:04:08,315 --> 00:04:09,474
Huh?

53
00:04:09,475 --> 00:04:13,265
Alright, let's begin today's lecture.

54
00:04:32,905 --> 00:04:34,405
Inuzuka.

55
00:04:44,375 --> 00:04:46,945
Why not start a new romance then?

56
00:04:47,185 --> 00:04:48,125
Huh?

57
00:04:48,126 --> 00:04:49,355
You're being too loud.

58
00:04:49,715 --> 00:04:51,625
Ah... sorry.

59
00:04:52,525 --> 00:04:54,885
That's what you get for saying
weird things out of nowhere.

60
00:04:54,945 --> 00:04:56,195
No, I mean...

61
00:04:56,425 --> 00:04:59,465
I was wondering if we should go to
this welcome party.

62
00:05:00,165 --> 00:05:01,165
Hm?

63
00:05:01,735 --> 00:05:05,865
(Looking for a new romance? We're the Light Music
Club!) The Light Music Club. That's for bands, right?

64
00:05:06,285 --> 00:05:07,285
I actually...

65
00:05:07,405 --> 00:05:09,175
was in a band back in high school.

66
00:05:09,205 --> 00:05:11,545
So I figured I'd keep playing in college.

67
00:05:15,545 --> 00:05:18,345
I might want to join too.

68
00:05:19,175 --> 00:05:20,175
Really?

69
00:05:21,025 --> 00:05:22,025
Yeah.

70
00:05:22,115 --> 00:05:25,785
I've never played an instrument,
but I listen to a lot of rock music.

71
00:05:26,525 --> 00:05:27,525
You do, Miwa?

72
00:05:27,525 --> 00:05:28,105
Yeah.

73
00:05:28,106 --> 00:05:29,455
That's so unexpected.

74
00:05:31,625 --> 00:05:32,795
I get it.

75
00:05:33,365 --> 00:05:35,235
You were influenced by an ex, weren't you?

76
00:05:35,265 --> 00:05:37,385
The complicated boyfriend
you were just talking about.

77
00:05:38,905 --> 00:05:41,505
He wasn't my boyfriend.

78
00:05:42,335 --> 00:05:43,575
He wasn't?

79
00:05:44,335 --> 00:05:46,275
I see. Wait.

80
00:05:46,445 --> 00:05:47,815
Did I guess wrong?

81
00:05:48,075 --> 00:05:49,115
Huh? Then who was it?

82
00:05:49,125 --> 00:05:50,125
Your dad?

83
00:05:56,245 --> 00:05:57,245
Play a card! Play a card!

84
00:05:57,255 --> 00:06:00,125
- I did, I did!
- Come on, keep playing!

85
00:06:00,425 --> 00:06:02,755
Let me think! Let me think!

86
00:06:03,185 --> 00:06:05,425
Did you hear that?

87
00:06:05,725 --> 00:06:06,365
Hm?

88
00:06:06,366 --> 00:06:08,694
We're forming a band with these guys.

89
00:06:08,695 --> 00:06:09,735
Huh? We are?

90
00:06:09,765 --> 00:06:12,705
Listen up, everyone!
Starting from here, we have Mikkun,

91
00:06:13,165 --> 00:06:14,735
Tsuruta, and Lucha.

92
00:06:16,075 --> 00:06:20,645
Ah, um, I'm Inuzuka Miwa.

93
00:06:22,115 --> 00:06:23,215
Nice to meet you all.

94
00:06:25,545 --> 00:06:26,644
Do you have a boyfriend, Miwa?

95
00:06:26,645 --> 00:06:27,864
Huh? What's your type?

96
00:06:27,865 --> 00:06:30,195
Wait. What kind of guy
do I have to be to date you?

97
00:06:30,525 --> 00:06:33,225
- You have zero chance.
- My bad.

98
00:06:33,425 --> 00:06:36,085
- You're definitely out of the running.
- That's not true!

99
00:06:36,145 --> 00:06:37,564
- I have a shot, right?
- Come on, tell us!

100
00:06:37,565 --> 00:06:38,565
Um...

101
00:06:39,695 --> 00:06:41,995
I don't have a boyfriend.

102
00:06:43,165 --> 00:06:45,065
As for my type...

103
00:06:46,105 --> 00:06:47,105
Sorry.

104
00:06:47,605 --> 00:06:50,274
- I don't really know either.
- Hey, come on!

105
00:06:50,275 --> 00:06:51,584
Wait, Miwa, you really don't have one?

106
00:06:51,585 --> 00:06:52,585
What do you mean you don't know?

107
00:06:52,586 --> 00:06:53,905
That's so surprising.

108
00:06:54,815 --> 00:06:55,815
Huh?

109
00:06:56,075 --> 00:06:57,015
- What about me?
- But honestly,

110
00:06:57,045 --> 00:06:59,144
- Pick me, pick me!
- Let a guy dream, will ya?

111
00:06:59,145 --> 00:07:00,315
No way.

112
00:07:00,715 --> 00:07:02,584
You guys are way too thirsty.

113
00:07:02,585 --> 00:07:05,384
Miwa is shy,
so give her a break.

114
00:07:05,385 --> 00:07:06,385
Right?

115
00:07:06,655 --> 00:07:08,095
- No way, that's you.
- No, it's not!

116
00:07:08,585 --> 00:07:09,945
Band name? What about a band name?

117
00:07:10,625 --> 00:07:13,395
No, it's because of what you just said.

118
00:07:15,635 --> 00:07:18,305
The welcome party was really fun.

119
00:07:18,325 --> 00:07:19,705
And we successfully formed a band.

120
00:07:20,265 --> 00:07:23,784
Um, Saeko, thank you.

121
00:07:23,785 --> 00:07:24,785
Huh?

122
00:07:24,905 --> 00:07:28,175
Thanks for bailing me out
when I didn't know what to say.

123
00:07:28,585 --> 00:07:31,845
You're just too easy to read, Miwa.

124
00:07:32,345 --> 00:07:36,115
Everyone has things
they don't want to be grilled about.

125
00:07:37,045 --> 00:07:39,661
Do you have things like that too, Saeko?
Things you don't want to talk about?

126
00:07:39,685 --> 00:07:41,425
Of course I do.

127
00:07:41,445 --> 00:07:42,445
Ah.

128
00:07:42,525 --> 00:07:44,355
You're laughing at me, aren't you?

129
00:07:44,445 --> 00:07:45,765
No, I'm not.

130
00:07:48,765 --> 00:07:51,945
I guess it's fine
if I tell you, Miwa.

131
00:07:51,985 --> 00:07:52,985
I might as well tell you.

132
00:07:56,505 --> 00:08:00,805
To be honest,
I'm not really into guys.

133
00:08:01,175 --> 00:08:03,415
I prefer girls.

134
00:08:06,885 --> 00:08:07,885
Huh?

135
00:08:10,155 --> 00:08:11,205
Ah, sorry.

136
00:08:11,255 --> 00:08:12,085
No, it's not that.

137
00:08:12,125 --> 00:08:15,925
I mean, I have dated guys before.

138
00:08:23,065 --> 00:08:24,165
Me too.

139
00:08:25,365 --> 00:08:26,365
Huh?

140
00:08:28,885 --> 00:08:32,445
I like girls.

141
00:08:34,464 --> 00:08:37,167
S-Seriously? You're not just
saying that to agree with me, right?

142
00:08:37,191 --> 00:08:39,891
I wouldn't lie about something like this.

143
00:08:43,445 --> 00:08:44,925
Seriously?

144
00:08:53,165 --> 00:08:54,165
Wow.

145
00:08:54,395 --> 00:08:55,395
Well, in that case,

146
00:08:56,085 --> 00:08:58,905
There's no time like the present.
Why don't we try going out?

147
00:09:01,045 --> 00:09:04,505
Huh? Because it's a rare opportunity?

148
00:09:04,545 --> 00:09:08,104
I mean, meeting someone else who likes
girls is practically a miracle, right?

149
00:09:08,105 --> 00:09:11,385
Besides, I wouldn't have said anything
if it were anyone but you, Miwa.

150
00:09:13,225 --> 00:09:18,955
Do you mean, um...
you like me?

151
00:09:19,525 --> 00:09:20,525
Huh?

152
00:09:20,725 --> 00:09:21,725
Huh...

153
00:09:22,225 --> 00:09:24,095
I-I guess so.

154
00:09:24,685 --> 00:09:27,625
Like, as a friend, I guess.

155
00:09:28,485 --> 00:09:29,845
Probably?

156
00:09:30,725 --> 00:09:34,124
Wait, what about you, Miwa?
Do you like me?

157
00:09:34,125 --> 00:09:35,335
Or do you hate me?

158
00:09:36,505 --> 00:09:38,344
That's not fair, asking it like that.

159
00:09:38,345 --> 00:09:41,775
Since we both like each other as friends,
wouldn't it be nice to try dating?

160
00:09:43,615 --> 00:09:44,615
Huh...

161
00:09:47,215 --> 00:09:49,355
Never mind all that.
Which is it?

162
00:09:49,465 --> 00:09:51,485
Are we dating? Or not?

163
00:09:56,725 --> 00:10:01,965
Sure. If it's you, Saeko,
I wouldn't mind going out with you.

164
00:10:02,625 --> 00:10:05,465
Awesome!

165
00:10:07,565 --> 00:10:10,475
I'm so happy I get to date you, Miwa.

166
00:10:10,765 --> 00:10:12,275
I promise I'll treat you right.

167
00:10:14,945 --> 00:10:16,675
Awesome!

168
00:10:25,745 --> 00:10:28,555
- So annoying.
- You're up next, Miwa.

169
00:10:29,025 --> 00:10:30,325
Saeko.

170
00:10:33,625 --> 00:10:35,335
Huh? Where's Mikkun?

171
00:10:35,725 --> 00:10:38,325
He said he was still hungry
and went to the school store.

172
00:10:41,105 --> 00:10:43,675
Hey, about our band's lead singer...

173
00:10:43,805 --> 00:10:47,384
I definitely think Miwa should do it.
Even though Lucha really wants the spot.

174
00:10:47,385 --> 00:10:48,965
Why?

175
00:10:48,985 --> 00:10:51,085
You haven't even heard me sing.

176
00:10:51,145 --> 00:10:52,344
Draw four.

177
00:10:52,345 --> 00:10:56,055
Because draw four.

178
00:10:58,425 --> 00:11:00,625
Miwa has more stage presence.

179
00:11:02,285 --> 00:11:05,625
I'm actually not a very good singer.

180
00:11:06,405 --> 00:11:07,465
Draw four.

181
00:11:08,705 --> 00:11:12,435
- Tsuru!
- You're just being modest.

182
00:11:12,465 --> 00:11:14,384
I really can't sing at all.

183
00:11:14,385 --> 00:11:15,935
Really?

184
00:11:16,675 --> 00:11:17,975
I don't know,

185
00:11:18,485 --> 00:11:20,245
Are you two sitting a little too close?

186
00:11:21,785 --> 00:11:22,915
Are we?

187
00:11:23,585 --> 00:11:24,585
Well...

188
00:11:24,685 --> 00:11:26,085
Right?

189
00:11:26,445 --> 00:11:27,585
Well what?

190
00:11:28,315 --> 00:11:32,485
Because we're good friends.

191
00:11:32,525 --> 00:11:34,425
Right?

192
00:11:35,225 --> 00:11:37,205
I guess so.

193
00:11:39,725 --> 00:11:43,264
The First Annual Lead Singer Showdown!
One round takes all, no hard feelings!

194
00:11:43,265 --> 00:11:45,905
The Ultimate Vocal Battle Royale!

195
00:11:47,245 --> 00:11:48,189
That's way too long.

196
00:11:48,213 --> 00:11:52,324
Too wordy. Is there even going to be a second
one? Anyway, I nominate Miwa for lead singer.

197
00:11:52,678 --> 00:11:53,776
Saeko...

198
00:11:53,800 --> 00:11:57,904
Having Miwa as the lead singer
does sound like a good idea.

199
00:11:57,905 --> 00:12:02,014
I get that, but what about my image?

200
00:12:02,015 --> 00:12:07,385
But girls always tell me I'm a
great singer! So please let me do it!

201
00:12:13,385 --> 00:12:16,025
Being too good at
singing is actually a turn-off.

202
00:12:17,095 --> 00:12:18,365
He sings so well.

203
00:12:20,925 --> 00:12:21,925
That's me.

204
00:12:24,385 --> 00:12:25,385
That's my song.

205
00:12:26,785 --> 00:12:28,604
- It's me! It's my song!
- I'm better, right?

206
00:12:28,605 --> 00:12:30,004
Saeko.

207
00:12:30,005 --> 00:12:31,385
What's wrong with that?

208
00:12:33,285 --> 00:12:34,785
Miwa, what are you going to sing?

209
00:12:35,815 --> 00:12:37,355
Well...

210
00:12:38,465 --> 00:12:39,955
What should I pick?

211
00:12:43,345 --> 00:12:48,345
♪ Swaying back and
forth, just like a dream ♪

212
00:12:48,925 --> 00:12:53,925
♪ Swaying back and
forth, slowly melting away ♪

213
00:12:59,905 --> 00:13:01,944
See? I told you.

214
00:13:01,945 --> 00:13:04,324
I'm not very good at this.

215
00:13:04,325 --> 00:13:08,905
No, no, no. Well, you see...

216
00:13:08,925 --> 00:13:10,504
I thought it was great.

217
00:13:10,505 --> 00:13:14,024
Hey, can't you guys give a normal reaction?

218
00:13:14,025 --> 00:13:16,155
No, it's just that Miwa...

219
00:13:16,325 --> 00:13:20,525
Miwa, don't worry about it.
Being tone-deaf is no big deal.

220
00:13:22,295 --> 00:13:23,435
Whatever. It's fine.

221
00:13:25,165 --> 00:13:26,805
Let's just sing together.

222
00:13:27,405 --> 00:13:29,165
♪ Doing it ♪

223
00:13:29,305 --> 00:13:32,925
♪ Because our pace is different, BPM ♪

224
00:13:33,025 --> 00:13:37,225
♪ Matching the 83 beat,
taking a night walk with you ♪

225
00:13:37,285 --> 00:13:40,445
♪ Don't say anymore ♪

226
00:13:40,505 --> 00:13:43,304
♪ Do you know about the
"chronostasis illusion"? ♪

227
00:13:43,305 --> 00:13:45,684
You say you don't know.

228
00:13:45,685 --> 00:13:47,555
She's so good...

229
00:13:50,145 --> 00:13:53,025
Wow, that's so cool.

230
00:13:54,935 --> 00:13:55,935
That's insane.

231
00:13:56,885 --> 00:13:58,635
So cool.

232
00:14:00,105 --> 00:14:03,034
So Lucha is the lead
singer, and Miwa is on bass.

233
00:14:03,035 --> 00:14:05,305
Can I really do this?

234
00:14:05,365 --> 00:14:07,575
I don't think I have any musical talent.

235
00:14:08,475 --> 00:14:09,975
You'll be fine.

236
00:14:10,005 --> 00:14:12,785
For bass, as long as you have a
sense of rhythm, you can play it.

237
00:14:13,615 --> 00:14:15,515
Your rhythm just now was pretty good.

238
00:14:16,105 --> 00:14:17,955
Only my rhythm, though.

239
00:14:20,125 --> 00:14:21,825
Doesn't this suit Miwa perfectly?

240
00:14:23,405 --> 00:14:25,125
So cute.

241
00:14:25,405 --> 00:14:26,525
Looks good.

242
00:14:26,865 --> 00:14:28,735
Let me test it out for you.

243
00:14:29,565 --> 00:14:30,565
Huh? Can you?

244
00:14:31,805 --> 00:14:32,805
Excuse me.

245
00:14:33,345 --> 00:14:36,484
Can I try playing that white one?

246
00:14:36,485 --> 00:14:37,585
Yes, of course.

247
00:14:49,645 --> 00:14:50,755
Don't fall for me.

248
00:14:54,525 --> 00:14:56,655
Say something, will you?

249
00:14:56,755 --> 00:14:58,025
See?

250
00:15:05,205 --> 00:15:07,065
- Miwa.
- Yeah?

251
00:15:07,825 --> 00:15:09,335
Let's hold hands.

252
00:15:09,985 --> 00:15:10,985
Huh?

253
00:15:11,865 --> 00:15:13,245
Out here on the street?

254
00:15:13,275 --> 00:15:15,145
No one's looking.

255
00:15:15,345 --> 00:15:16,915
Plus, they're all strangers anyway.

256
00:15:20,065 --> 00:15:21,255
I guess it's fine.

257
00:15:32,125 --> 00:15:33,595
Saeko.

258
00:15:34,285 --> 00:15:36,895
Are you the really open type?

259
00:15:37,105 --> 00:15:41,365
Maybe I am.

260
00:15:42,705 --> 00:15:44,945
I mean, I've always been like this.

261
00:15:46,305 --> 00:15:49,215
But now I've decided to just
live my life without holding back.

262
00:15:52,325 --> 00:15:57,715
I used to struggle with having to
conform to society's expectations.

263
00:15:58,355 --> 00:16:01,125
But eventually, I realized
how stupid that was.

264
00:16:03,305 --> 00:16:04,405
Because I don't want...

265
00:16:04,525 --> 00:16:06,565
...a life full of holding back.

266
00:16:11,565 --> 00:16:12,605
What's wrong?

267
00:16:13,795 --> 00:16:14,795
Ah.

268
00:16:15,065 --> 00:16:16,075
Nothing.

269
00:16:17,385 --> 00:16:22,745
It's just the first time you've said
something so serious, Saeko. It surprised me.

270
00:16:23,745 --> 00:16:25,615
Oh, come on. What are you talking about?

271
00:16:26,985 --> 00:16:30,385
But I think I get it.

272
00:16:31,325 --> 00:16:34,525
Maybe we think the same way.

273
00:16:36,095 --> 00:16:39,345
We both want to live without
betraying our true feelings, right?

274
00:16:42,365 --> 00:16:43,365
Yeah.

275
00:17:14,105 --> 00:17:15,425
Saeko.

276
00:17:15,465 --> 00:17:16,465
Um...

277
00:17:17,265 --> 00:17:18,265
Yeah?

278
00:17:19,565 --> 00:17:20,565
Well...

279
00:17:21,475 --> 00:17:24,275
When you confessed to me before...

280
00:17:25,145 --> 00:17:27,605
...didn't you say you didn't
really see me that way?

281
00:17:28,245 --> 00:17:31,745
What about now?

282
00:17:32,725 --> 00:17:34,564
Huh? What?

283
00:17:34,565 --> 00:17:36,085
What's wrong? Why the sudden question?

284
00:17:38,065 --> 00:17:42,645
I want to know if your "like" feelings
have changed from friend to girlfriend.

285
00:17:45,025 --> 00:17:46,965
Why do you ask?

286
00:17:49,505 --> 00:17:53,935
I've always wanted a girlfriend.

287
00:17:53,965 --> 00:17:58,225
So when you said we should
date, I was really happy.

288
00:18:00,885 --> 00:18:03,815
But, how should I put it...

289
00:18:05,145 --> 00:18:11,485
It feels like we're only dating
out of compromise or convenience.

290
00:18:13,365 --> 00:18:16,795
Miwa, what exactly are you trying to say?

291
00:18:17,045 --> 00:18:18,045
Ah.

292
00:18:18,565 --> 00:18:19,565
Well...

293
00:18:20,895 --> 00:18:28,575
Basically, I don't know if this is how
love and dating are supposed to be.

294
00:18:28,905 --> 00:18:30,205
So I'm a bit confused.

295
00:18:30,705 --> 00:18:32,905
You're so serious, Miwa.

296
00:18:34,575 --> 00:18:37,475
My heart races when you touch me.

297
00:18:38,045 --> 00:18:42,085
But whether that's out of
romantic feelings or not...

298
00:18:45,555 --> 00:18:46,955
...I'm not sure.

299
00:18:49,455 --> 00:18:50,455
Listen.

300
00:18:51,175 --> 00:18:54,195
If you're thinking this
seriously about us...

301
00:18:54,265 --> 00:18:56,765
...doesn't that mean you already like me?

302
00:18:57,495 --> 00:18:58,574
Huh?

303
00:18:58,575 --> 00:19:00,765
I mean, you definitely like me, right?

304
00:19:03,575 --> 00:19:04,575
Eh.

305
00:19:05,315 --> 00:19:08,075
Does dating have to be so rigid?

306
00:19:08,595 --> 00:19:11,045
If it doesn't work out, we
can just break up, right?

307
00:19:12,715 --> 00:19:14,454
Why are you so casual about this?

308
00:19:14,455 --> 00:19:16,055
What's wrong with being a little casual?

309
00:19:16,355 --> 00:19:19,314
Can't we just try dating first?

310
00:19:19,315 --> 00:19:20,415
When it comes to love...

311
00:19:22,635 --> 00:19:26,395
Are you forcing yourself, Saeko?

312
00:19:28,015 --> 00:19:29,235
Not at all.

313
00:19:29,855 --> 00:19:32,775
But if you want to break
up, Miwa, I'll go along with it.

314
00:19:33,475 --> 00:19:38,675
But right now, I have absolutely
no intention of breaking up.

315
00:19:42,375 --> 00:19:45,445
I don't want to break up either.

316
00:19:46,875 --> 00:19:50,685
But when it comes to the confession...

317
00:19:50,915 --> 00:19:53,285
...I want a do-over.

318
00:19:53,625 --> 00:19:55,314
Why?

319
00:19:55,315 --> 00:19:58,795
I feel like I was acting too
high and mighty back then.

320
00:19:59,675 --> 00:20:01,265
I've been regretting it.

321
00:20:04,795 --> 00:20:06,035
What?

322
00:20:09,475 --> 00:20:10,475
Saeko.

323
00:20:13,805 --> 00:20:14,805
Yeah?

324
00:20:20,015 --> 00:20:21,255
Let's go out.

325
00:20:26,555 --> 00:20:27,555
Okay.

326
00:20:27,635 --> 00:20:29,125
I wouldn't mind dating you.

327
00:20:37,595 --> 00:20:39,074
Were you just nervous?

328
00:20:39,075 --> 00:20:40,755
Huh? No way.

329
00:20:53,515 --> 00:20:55,475
No way, I definitely can't play this.

330
00:20:56,015 --> 00:20:58,025
As a beginner, I actually...

331
00:20:58,975 --> 00:21:01,429
Miwa, want to practice together? We're
both in the rhythm section, after all.

332
00:21:01,453 --> 00:21:03,834
Practice with me. I've
played bass before, at least.

333
00:21:03,835 --> 00:21:04,835
Me too! Me too! Me too!

334
00:21:04,935 --> 00:21:05,975
You guys can pass.

335
00:21:06,035 --> 00:21:08,335
Lucha, you've never even played before.

336
00:21:08,435 --> 00:21:11,905
Alright, shut up. You're bothering Miwa.

337
00:21:12,615 --> 00:21:14,034
This has nothing to do with you, Saeko.

338
00:21:14,035 --> 00:21:15,805
Of course it does. I'm...

339
00:21:17,605 --> 00:21:18,605
Huh?

340
00:21:21,715 --> 00:21:22,715
I'm...

341
00:21:23,075 --> 00:21:25,385
...Miwa's bass master.

342
00:21:26,045 --> 00:21:27,115
Master?

343
00:21:27,715 --> 00:21:28,785
Is that so?

344
00:21:29,885 --> 00:21:31,055
I guess so.

345
00:21:32,475 --> 00:21:34,515
By the way, shouldn't you
guys be heading to class?

346
00:21:35,795 --> 00:21:38,215
Hurry up and get out.

347
00:21:38,975 --> 00:21:40,775
- Hurry up.
- Get ready, quick.

348
00:21:41,255 --> 00:21:43,355
- Move it.
- Stop dawdling.

349
00:21:44,165 --> 00:21:45,305
Saeko.

350
00:21:46,895 --> 00:21:48,095
Aren't you going to tell them?

351
00:21:49,475 --> 00:21:51,015
Well...

352
00:21:51,975 --> 00:21:55,045
If you tell the wrong people,
things can get pretty ugly...

353
00:21:57,815 --> 00:22:00,535
Lucha, you're still dragging your feet.

354
00:22:01,095 --> 00:22:03,955
- Hurry up.
- We're going to be late again.

355
00:22:05,655 --> 00:22:09,095
Saeko, how do I position my fingers here?

356
00:22:10,455 --> 00:22:12,725
- You hold it down here...
- Yeah.

357
00:22:30,035 --> 00:22:31,035
Miwa.

358
00:22:54,935 --> 00:22:56,305
Wait a minute.

359
00:22:57,475 --> 00:22:58,974
We're in the club room.

360
00:22:58,975 --> 00:23:00,735
Who cares? No one's looking.

361
00:23:01,755 --> 00:23:03,555
That's not the point.

362
00:23:04,575 --> 00:23:05,575
There should be more...

363
00:23:05,895 --> 00:23:06,895
...mood or something.

364
00:23:07,915 --> 00:23:08,915
Miwa.

365
00:23:09,695 --> 00:23:11,515
Don't tell me this is your first time?

366
00:23:15,455 --> 00:23:16,755
I don't know.

367
00:23:20,595 --> 00:23:21,635
Shut up.

368
00:23:43,255 --> 00:23:46,655
Ah, sorry. I accidentally saw that.

369
00:23:50,595 --> 00:23:52,064
(Next Episode)
One-month anniversary.

370
00:23:52,065 --> 00:23:53,495
Congratulations.

371
00:23:53,535 --> 00:23:55,874
I want to join this club.

372
00:23:55,875 --> 00:23:58,754
I really feel like we've been
missing each other lately.

373
00:23:58,755 --> 00:24:00,155
You think it's a hassle, don't you?

374
00:24:00,405 --> 00:24:01,405
Dealing with me.

375
00:24:02,815 --> 00:24:04,335
I want all of you, Miwa.

